"{\"tool\": \"search\", \"arguments\": {\"query\": \"brand\", \"path\": \"apps/canvas\"}}"
"Summary of earlier turns: I made one tool call, search with query \"brand\" under path apps/canvas. The output was long (about 59k characters, truncated in display) and had these main groups of hits:\n\n- apps/canvas/design/legacy-console-reference.html and legality-screen-reference.html: static design references with CSS for a .brand block (logo tile, gradient, bold name, small subtitle). These are mockups, not app code.\n- apps/canvas/src/brand.ts: the wire-format parser for the airline brand. It exports TENANT_LOGO = \"/api/auth/brand/logo\", NEUTRAL_MARK and parseBrand. It accepts only same-origin URLs matching /^\\/api\\/auth\\/brand\\/(logo|wordmark|wordmark-white|hero)(\\?v=[A-Za-z0-9]{1,64})?$/. Anything else is ignored into a \"no brand\" state that shows the tenant name and the neutral dCortex mark, never another airline's. It cites knowledge-base/features/tenant-branding.md.\n- apps/canvas/src/brand.test.ts: tests for parseBrand. They cover valid descriptors, rejection of path traversal, unknown kinds, script injection and external URLs, hero focal and alt handling, the TENANT_LOGO constant, and that public/ has no tenant-logo file.\n- apps/canvas/src/ConsoleControls.tsx and ConsoleControls.test.tsx: imports NEUTRAL_MARK and TENANT_LOGO from brand.js. It defines the legacy-parity brand block (consoleBrand) passed to Shell as `brand`, and consoleLogo, which renders an img with src /api/auth/brand/logo. The BFF serves that logo per deployment.\n- apps/canvas/src/desk/briefModel.test.ts and swapModel.test.ts: only incidental matches on \"brand_new_*\" test strings, not relevant.\n- apps/canvas/src/i18n/messages.ts: many i18n keys in English, Spanish and French. These include landing.brand (\"dCortex\"), ops.brand (\"{customer} Operations\") and the whole tenantConfig.brand.* group for the admin Branding screen. That group covers title, subtitle, kinds (logo, wordmark, wordmarkWhite, hero), help text, source labels (admin, shipped, none), upload, replace and reset actions, previews, hero framing (alt, focal x/y), error messages, and BFF_BRAND_* error-code messages. The display cut off partway through the French block (around line 7680).\n\nNo files were opened or edited yet. Findings so far: the brand feature lives in apps/canvas/src/brand.ts, ConsoleControls.tsx and the tenantConfig.brand.* i18n keys. The server side (/api/auth/brand/*, BFF_BRAND_* codes) is outside apps/canvas and was not searched. The ticket text itself is not in the part of the conversation I can see, so the exact fix target is still undetermined."
